course: dictionary
lesson: 8289
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, so you must use context to choose the right one. The words around riser give you the clues. Riser can mean a person, a step part, a platform, or a pipe.
explain: «They may pick up news of Portly from early risers.» Here early risers are people who get up at dawn. The word early tells you a riser is someone who gets out of bed. Try your meaning in the sentence: "people who get up early" fits perfectly.
explain: On stairs, the riser is the upright piece between one tread (the part you step on) and the next. In a school concert, choir risers are low platforms that lift the singers up so everyone can be seen.
fact: A riser can be a person who gets up from bed at a certain time.
fact: «Early riser» means someone who wakes up early, and «late riser» means someone who gets up late.
fact: The riser of a staircase is the upright part between one step and the next.
fact: Choir risers are low platforms that make singers stand higher.
fact: Early risers are sometimes called "larks", like the birds that sing at dawn; people who stay up late are "night owls".
exercise: «They may pick up news of Portly from early risers.» In this sentence, what is an early riser? | A pipe going up a building | *A person who gets up early | A person who sleeps until noon | A step on a staircase
exercise: Dad says, «I am a late riser.» What does late riser mean? | A low platform for singers | A person who works at night | Someone who sleeps in the day | *A person who gets up late
exercise: On a staircase, what is the riser? | The pipe under the stairs | The rope at the side | *The upright part between one step and the next | The flat part you stand on
test: In a school concert, what are risers used for? | Seats for the parents | A place to store the music | Lights that shine on the stage | *Low platforms that lift the singers up
test: Which word is used in the sentence for early risers? | *Lark | Tread | Pipe | Night owl
exam: Which meaning of riser fits «He is an early riser, up before the birds»? | *A person who gets up from bed at a certain time | The upright part of a step | A pipe going up a building | A low stage block
